  "definition": "Domestication is the process by which wild organisms give rise to cultivated forms through human-associated selection and breeding. In this packet, it refers to the origin of cultivated bananas from wild relatives, with diversity also expanding after initial domestication through later hybridization and introgression from local wild populations.",
